        <body>
            <div xml:id="d617">

                <pb facs="1086" n="992" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg992"/>

                <head>No. 617.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Curry.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-03-29"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 29,
                        1887</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 182.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose for your information a copy of a
                    dispatch from our consul-general at Havana, concerning an exaction of
                    differential duties in January last, at Havana, on the cargo of the American
                    bark <hi rendition="#italic">Sarah A. Staples.</hi></p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F. Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>




